doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19025338
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
abstract: >-
  HTTP REST bridge for bHaptics haptic hardware. Wraps the bhaptics-python SDK in a small aiohttp server so that any language can drive bHaptics vests, arm bands and gloves over plain HTTP, with raw per-motor control and no bHaptics Studio registration. Accepts motor values as a plain list of intensities or as sparse index/intensity entries, needs no bHaptics API key for haptics, reports which devices are connected (live with a key), and is documented against bHaptics' own SDK reference. Runs on the Windows machine where bHaptics Player runs.
keywords:
  - haptics
  - bHaptics
  - REST API
  - bridge
  - TactSuit
  - wearable computing
  - tactile feedback
  - virtual reality
